{
  "description": "The key and guardrail routes declare a single 404 (`NotFound`, body `{ error: { code: 404, message: \"Resource not found\" } }`) whose only subject is the resource named in the path: GET/PATCH/DELETE /keys/{hash} -> the key, GET/PATCH/DELETE /guardrails/{id} and GET /guardrails/{id}/assignments/{keys,members} -> the guardrail (\"Guardrail not found, or the workspace default guardrail has not been configured yet.\"). Replace that NotFound with resource-specific KeyNotFound / GuardrailNotFound so callers can tell which resource is gone. The bulk assign/unassign routes (POST /guardrails/{id}/assignments/...) keep the generic NotFound: their 404 can name either the guardrail or a key/member in the body (a just-created key briefly 404s on assignment, observed by alchemy's OpenRouter.Guardrail), and the response carries no discriminator. Source: OpenRouter OpenAPI spec (404 responses and examples), 2026-10-06; not probed live (no OpenRouter management key available).",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.openrouter.api#KeyNotFound",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
          "message": {
            "target": "smithy.api#String"
          }
        },
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#error": "client",
          "smithy.api#httpError": 404,
          "smithy.api#documentation": "No API key with this hash exists (or it was deleted).",
          "com.distilled.openapi#errorMatchers": [
            {
              "status": 404
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.openrouter.api#GuardrailNotFound",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
          "message": {
            "target": "smithy.api#String"
          }
        },
        "traits": {
          "smithy.api#error": "client",
          "smithy.api#httpError": 404,
          "smithy.api#documentation": "No guardrail with this id exists (or it was deleted).",
          "com.distilled.openapi#errorMatchers": [
            {
              "status": 404
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/shapes/com.openrouter.api#GetKey/errors/1",
      "value": {
        "target": "com.openrouter.api#NotFound"
      }
    },
    {
